#!/bin/sh
# Copyright (c) 2026 Jiaxing Hu <gahing@gahingwoo.com>
# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2026-08-25 round 379. THE ENERGY BASELINE. MEASURE, DO NOT DESIGN.
#
# 🏁 ROUND 378 was a clean regression and it repeated clean a second time:
#
#            r378        repeat      delta
#   64 tok   14.70       14.58       -0.82%
#   384 tok  11.98       11.92       -0.50%
#   control  14.01       13.92       -0.64%
#
# ⚠ All five deltas came out the SAME SIGN. Pure noise does not do that five
# times, so what we have is a small per-boot offset rather than jitter. The
# band is <= 1%; a repeat landing half a percent slow is not a finding.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY THIS ROUND EXISTS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The next piece of work is a power-save mode and a performance mode for a
# BATTERY device. Before designing either, the honest question is what
# actually drains the battery. Every round in this project that guessed first
# had to be taken back.
#
# ⚠ THERE IS NO POWER METER, AND THIS BOARD CANNOT MAKE ONE. rock-4d.dts has
# no ina2xx, no ina3221, no shunt, no fuel gauge, no battery -- checked. So
# absolute watts are not available at any price, and nothing in this round
# claims them. What IS available is RESIDENCY, and a mode decision needs a
# RATIO, not a wattage:
#
#   * cpuidle time per core        -- how long each core was actually asleep
#   * cpufreq time_in_state        -- which OPP each cluster sat at
#   * runtime_suspended_time       -- whether the NPU cores really suspended
#   * six thermal zones            -- bigcore, littlecore, npu, ddr separately
#
# runtime_status / runtime_active_time / runtime_suspended_time are in the
# UNCONDITIONAL sysfs group (drivers/base/power/sysfs.c, before the
# CONFIG_PM_ADVANCED_DEBUG ifdef), so they read today with no rebuild.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TWO SUSPICIONS ALREADY CLOSED, FOR FREE, BEFORE THE BOARD RAN
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# ⛔ "sync_state() pending leaves power domains up" -- REFUTED. I said this
#    was genpd's defined behaviour and it is not. The rockchip pmdomain driver
#    sets GENPD_FLAG_NO_STAY_ON, and core.c does
#        genpd->stay_on = !genpd_is_no_stay_on(genpd) && !is_off;
#    so those domains are never held on waiting for sync_state, and
#    genpd_power_off_unused() runs at late_initcall_sync regardless. r378's
#    own log has "PM: genpd: Disabling unused power domains" at t=1.35s and
#    "vdd_gpu_s0: disabling". The pending lines are noise.
#
# ⛔ "the idle worker pool spins" -- REFUTED. llama.c's worker blocks in
#    pthread_cond_wait. Idle threads cost nothing.
#
# ✅ ONE REAL LEAD SURVIVES, and it is in our own cmdline:
#        console=ttyS0,1500000n8 ... rootwait rw clk_ignore_unused log_buf_len=8M
#    clk_ignore_unused was a bring-up crutch. It forbids gating EVERY clock the
#    bootloader left running. That is not tested here -- dropping it risks the
#    NPU and would cost the whole round -- but this round counts how many
#    clocks are enabled with no user, which says whether the crutch is
#    expensive before anyone risks removing it.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE QUESTION THIS ROUND ANSWERS: A53 OR A72?
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The kernel's own energy model, from rk3576.dtsi:
#
#   cluster0  A53 x4  dynamic-power-coefficient = 120   2016 MHz @ 0.900 V
#   cluster1  A72 x4  dynamic-power-coefficient = 320   2208 MHz @ 0.925 V
#
#   P = coeff * f(MHz) * V^2  ->  A53 196 mW/core, A72 605 mW/core = 3.09x
#   At an OPP both share (1200 MHz @ 0.700 V) it is 70.6 vs 188 mW = 2.67x.
#
# charsiu uses ONE CPU thread's worth of work, so where it runs is a threefold
# question on a battery. ⚠ Memory said this was CLOSED, and memory was reading
# the wrong axis: the 0.3 ms from round 368 was PINNED vs UNPINNED, and
# unpinned the scheduler had already put it on a big core. The A53 arm has
# never run. It is also nearly free, because CHARSIU_CPUS exists and
# cpus_pin() is called before pthread_create, so the workers inherit the mask.
#
# ⚠ WHAT WOULD MAKE THE A53 LOSE: the CPU stages are SERIAL with the NPU
# fence, so a slower core lengthens the token, and the NPU rail is then up for
# longer. Slower-but-cheaper is not automatically cheaper. This round measures
# both halves and decides nothing.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HOW TO READ IT
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   * arm 0 is DISCARDED. It only warms the page cache. In r378 the first run
#     staged in 24159 ms and every later one in about 7900 -- a 3x difference
#     that would swamp any comparison between arms 2 and 3.
#   * arm 1 is the idle floor. Both clusters should be near 100% idle
#     residency and BOTH NPU CORES SHOULD READ suspended.
#   * arms 2 and 3 are the same 64 tokens, pinned to 4-7 and to 0-3. Compare
#     tok/s, then compare the two clusters' time_in_state and their tsadc.
#     ⚠ Their power deltas cover load + staging + prompt + generation, not
#     generation alone. That is fair between the two arms because both have
#     the same phases, and it is NOT a per-token energy number.
#   * arm 4 holds 20 s with the model resident and nobody talking. This is
#     where a battery device actually lives. THE FALSIFIABLE CLAUSE:
#     rocket takes a runtime-PM reference per job with a 50 ms autosuspend
#     delay, so over a 20 s hold both cores must read suspended and
#     runtime_suspended_time must advance by about 20000 ms. If it does not,
#     that is the finding of the round.
#   * probe exact, anchor clean.
#
# NOTHING IS OPTIMISED THIS ROUND. Arm 2 must land in r378's band.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
NPU_DIR=/opt/npu-test
C=/dev/console
WORK=/usr/lib/libteflon-working.so
VD=/opt/charsiu/charsiu_vendor
V=/opt/charsiu/vendor
RGC=$V/vendor-int4-k2048-n1024.regcmd
WT=$V/vendor-wt-1M.bin
IN=$V/vendor-in.bin
RUN=/opt/charsiu/charsiu_run
M8=/opt/charsiu/models/Llama-3.2-1B-Instruct-Q8_0.gguf
PROMPT="The capital of France is"
LIMIT=420
NGEN=64
CE=CHARSIU_COEF_ELEMS=65536
HEAD=CHARSIU_NPU_MAXN=131072
ABORT=0
log() { echo "$@" > "$C"; }
nbad() { dmesg 2>/dev/null | grep -c "MMU_DTE_ADDR\|job timed out"; }

health() {
	python3 "$NPU_DIR/perch.py" "$NPU_DIR/conv2d-cal.tflite" > /tmp/hc.txt 2>&1
	if grep -q "128/128 channels match" /tmp/hc.txt; then
		log "  !! health OK, the block recovered, continuing"
	else
		log "  !! health FAILED, the block did not come back this time."
		ABORT=1
	fi
}

capped() {
	lim="$1"; shift
	"$@" &
	pid=$!
	i=0
	while [ "$i" -lt "$lim" ]; do
		kill -0 "$pid" 2>/dev/null || { wait "$pid"; return $?; }
		sleep 1
		i=$((i + 1))
	done
	kill -9 "$pid" 2>/dev/null
	wait "$pid" 2>/dev/null
	return 124
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE INSTRUMENT. No meter exists, so everything here is residency, and every
# line is a DELTA over a named window. Absolute counters are meaningless: they
# have been running since boot.
#
# Each sample line is  kind<TAB>key<TAB>value, and the kind carries the UNIT,
# because the four sources do not agree on one:
#   us   cpuidle time            microseconds
#   cs   cpufreq time_in_state   centiseconds (USER_HZ)
#   ms   runtime_*_time          milliseconds
#   temp thermal_zone temp       millidegrees
#   str  runtime_status          a word
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
psnap() {
	f="$1"; : > "$f"
	for z in /sys/class/thermal/thermal_zone*; do
		[ -r "$z/temp" ] || continue
		printf 'temp\t%s\t%s\n' "$(cat $z/type)" "$(cat $z/temp)" >> "$f"
	done
	for c in /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu0 /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu1 \
		 /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu2 /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu3 \
		 /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu4 /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu5 \
		 /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu6 /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu7; do
		n=${c##*/}
		for s in "$c"/cpuidle/state*; do
			[ -r "$s/time" ] || continue
			printf 'us\tidle.%s.%s\t%s\n' "$n" "$(cat $s/name)" \
				"$(cat $s/time)" >> "$f"
		done
	done
	for p in /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy*; do
		[ -r "$p/stats/time_in_state" ] || continue
		pn=${p##*/}
		awk -v pn="$pn" '{printf "cs\tfreq.%s.%s\t%s\n", pn, $1, $2}' \
			"$p/stats/time_in_state" >> "$f"
	done
	for d in /sys/bus/platform/devices/27700000.npu \
		 /sys/bus/platform/devices/27708000.npu; do
		[ -d "$d/power" ] || continue
		n=${d##*/}
		printf 'str\tnpu.%s.status\t%s\n' "$n" \
			"$(cat $d/power/runtime_status 2>/dev/null)" >> "$f"
		printf 'ms\tnpu.%s.active\t%s\n' "$n" \
			"$(cat $d/power/runtime_active_time 2>/dev/null)" >> "$f"
		printf 'ms\tnpu.%s.suspended\t%s\n' "$n" \
			"$(cat $d/power/runtime_suspended_time 2>/dev/null)" >> "$f"
	done
	printf 'wall\twall\t%s\n' "$(cut -d. -f1 /proc/uptime)" >> "$f"
}

# pdelta <before> <after> <label>
pdelta() {
	w1=$(awk -F'\t' '$2=="wall"{print $3}' "$2")
	w0=$(awk -F'\t' '$2=="wall"{print $3}' "$1")
	win=$((w1 - w0)); [ "$win" -lt 1 ] && win=1
	log ""
	log "  ~~ residency over $win s: $3"
	awk -F'\t' -v win="$win" '
	  NR==FNR { a[$2]=$3; next }
	  {
	    k=$1; key=$2; v=$3; o=a[key];
	    if (k=="temp")
		printf "     %-32s %7.1f C   (was %.1f)\n", key, v/1000, o/1000;
	    else if (k=="us")
		printf "     %-32s %7.2f s   %5.1f%%\n", key, (v-o)/1e6, (v-o)/(win*1e4);
	    else if (k=="cs")
		printf "     %-32s %7.2f s   %5.1f%%\n", key, (v-o)/100, (v-o)/win;
	    else if (k=="ms")
		printf "     %-32s %7.2f s   %5.1f%%\n", key, (v-o)/1e3, (v-o)/(win*10);
	    else if (k=="str")
		printf "     %-32s %7s     %s\n", key, v, (v==o ? "" : "(was " o ")");
	  }' "$1" "$2" > "$C"
}

# a window of pure nothing
idlewin() {
	psnap /tmp/p0
	sleep "$1"
	psnap /tmp/p1
	pdelta /tmp/p0 /tmp/p1 "$2"
}

rung() {
	[ "$ABORT" = "1" ] && { log "  -- SKIPPED (round aborted): $1"; return 0; }
	lbl="$1"; shift
	before=$(nbad)
	log ""
	log "  -- $lbl"
	sleep 1
	capped "$LIMIT" env "$@" "$RUN" "$M8" -p "$PROMPT" -n "${NGEN:-32}" \
		--ignore-eos -q -c 512 -t 4 > "$C" 2>&1
	rc=$?
	[ "$rc" != "0" ] && log "  !! the rung exited $rc (124 is the wall clock limit)"
	[ "$(nbad)" != "$before" ] && { log "  !! POISON. This rung is VOID."; health; }
	return 0
}

# the same rung, with a residency window wrapped round it
prung() {
	lbl="$1"
	psnap /tmp/p0
	rung "$@"
	psnap /tmp/p1
	pdelta /tmp/p0 /tmp/p1 "$lbl"
}

# generate, then sit there with everything still open, and sample the SITTING
holdarm() {
	[ "$ABORT" = "1" ] && { log "  -- SKIPPED (round aborted): $1"; return 0; }
	lbl="$1"; shift
	log ""
	log "  -- $lbl"
	sleep 1
	env "$@" "$RUN" "$M8" -p "$PROMPT" -n 32 --ignore-eos -q -c 512 -t 4 \
		--hold-secs 26 > /tmp/hold.txt 2>&1 &
	hpid=$!
	# wait for the hold to actually begin, up to 300 s of load+stage+generate
	i=0
	while [ "$i" -lt 300 ]; do
		grep -q "holding" /tmp/hold.txt 2>/dev/null && break
		kill -0 "$hpid" 2>/dev/null || break
		sleep 1
		i=$((i + 1))
	done
	if ! grep -q "holding" /tmp/hold.txt 2>/dev/null; then
		log "  !! the hold never started, this arm is VOID"
		wait "$hpid" 2>/dev/null
		cat /tmp/hold.txt > "$C"
		return 0
	fi
	# a moment for the last job to retire, then a clean 20 s of nothing
	sleep 3
	psnap /tmp/p0
	sleep 20
	psnap /tmp/p1
	wait "$hpid" 2>/dev/null
	grep -E "^\[|holding|hold done" /tmp/hold.txt > "$C"
	pdelta /tmp/p0 /tmp/p1 "$lbl"
	return 0
}

# arm: <label> <regcmd-or-dash> <byte> <high> [extra env, one assignment]
arm() {
	before=$(nbad)
	log ""
	log "  ---- $1"
	sleep 1
	env ${5:-IGNORED=1} $VD "$2" "$WT" "$IN" "$3" "$4" 4096 > /tmp/vd.txt 2>&1
	cat /tmp/vd.txt > "$C"
	after=$(nbad)
	if [ "$after" != "$before" ]; then
		log "  !! POISONED: $((after - before)) new fault or timeout lines"
		health
		ABORT=0
		sleep 2
	fi
}

start() {
	log ""
	log "###############################################################"
	log "##### round 379: the energy baseline, and A53 vs A72        #####"
	log "###############################################################"
	log "  no optimisation. arm 2 must land in r378's band."
	log "  there is NO POWER METER on this board and none is claimed;"
	log "  every number below is RESIDENCY over a named window."

	B="CHARSIU_NPU_QUANT=1 CHARSIU_NPU=1 CHARSIU_NPU_W4V=1 CHARSIU_NPU_KMAX=1024 CHARSIU_NPU_W4_GROUP=1024 CHARSIU_STAGES=1"

	log ""
	log "===== 0) the instrument, and the clock crutch                  ====="
	log "  what the board actually offers, once."
	log "  -- cpu policies"
	for p in /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy*; do
		[ -d "$p" ] || continue
		log "     ${p##*/}: cpus=$(cat $p/related_cpus 2>/dev/null) cur=$(cat $p/scaling_cur_freq 2>/dev/null) gov=$(cat $p/scaling_governor 2>/dev/null)"
	done
	log "  -- cpuidle states on cpu0 and cpu4"
	for s in /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu0/cpuidle/state* \
		 /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu4/cpuidle/state*; do
		[ -r "$s/name" ] || continue
		log "     $s -> $(cat $s/name) latency $(cat $s/latency 2>/dev/null) us"
	done
	log "  -- npu regulator"
	for r in /sys/class/regulator/regulator.*; do
		[ -r "$r/name" ] || continue
		nm=$(cat $r/name)
		case "$nm" in vdd_npu*|vdd_gpu*|vdd_cpu*)
			log "     $nm: state=$(cat $r/state 2>/dev/null) uV=$(cat $r/microvolts 2>/dev/null)" ;;
		esac
	done
	log "  -- clk_ignore_unused is on the cmdline. how many clocks does it hold?"
	mount -t debugfs none /sys/kernel/debug 2>/dev/null
	if [ -r /sys/kernel/debug/clk/clk_summary ]; then
		tot=$(awk 'NR>2 && NF>3 {n++} END {print n+0}' /sys/kernel/debug/clk/clk_summary)
		en=$(awk 'NR>2 && NF>3 && $2+0 > 0 {n++} END {print n+0}' /sys/kernel/debug/clk/clk_summary)
		nouser=$(awk 'NR>2 && NF>3 && $2+0 > 0 && $3+0 == 0 {n++} END {print n+0}' /sys/kernel/debug/clk/clk_summary)
		log "     $tot clocks, $en enabled, $nouser of those with NO prepare user"
		log "     (the last number is what dropping the crutch would go after)"
	else
		log "     clk_summary not available (debugfs did not mount)"
	fi

	log ""
	log "===== 1) THE IDLE FLOOR: 20 s of nothing                       ====="
	log "  both clusters near 100% idle, and BOTH NPU CORES suspended."
	idlewin 20 "idle floor, nothing running"

	log ""
	log "===== 0b) warm the page cache. THIS ARM IS DISCARDED.          ====="
	log "  r378 staged in 24159 ms cold and 7900 warm. Without this the"
	log "  comparison between arms 2 and 3 would measure the disk."
	rung "warm-up, discarded" $B "$CE" "$HEAD" CHARSIU_CPUS=4-7

	log ""
	log "===== 2) 64 tokens PINNED TO THE A72s (cpu4-7)                 ====="
	log "  the standing anchor. about 14.6 tok/s, the Louvre sentence."
	prung "64 tok on the A72s" "int4 g1024, CHARSIU_CPUS=4-7" $B "$CE" "$HEAD" CHARSIU_CPUS=4-7

	log ""
	log "===== 3) 64 tokens PINNED TO THE A53s (cpu0-3)                 ====="
	log "  THE QUESTION. Same work, a cluster the energy model prices at"
	log "  a third. Read tok/s first, then the two clusters' time_in_state."
	log "  The text must be the SAME SENTENCE -- affinity cannot move a bit."
	prung "64 tok on the A53s" "int4 g1024, CHARSIU_CPUS=0-3" $B "$CE" "$HEAD" CHARSIU_CPUS=0-3

	log ""
	log "===== 4) AN IDLE SESSION: model resident, nobody talking       ====="
	log "  20 s sampled while charsiu holds the model and the NPU fds."
	log "  FALSIFIABLE: rocket autosuspends 50 ms after the last job, so"
	log "  both cores must read suspended and suspended_time must advance"
	log "  by about 20000 ms. If it does not, that is the round's finding."
	holdarm "idle with the model resident" $B "$CE" "$HEAD" CHARSIU_CPUS=4-7

	log ""
	log "===== 5) the probe, still exact                                ====="
	arm "solo verify" "-" 0 0 "CHARSIU_M=1 CHARSIU_GEN=1 CHARSIU_VERIFY=1 CHARSIU_OUT_KB=64"

	log ""
	log "===== 6) the anchor: int8 conv must still be exact             ====="
	health

	log ""
	log "===== read arm 3's tok/s and arm 4's suspended_time first.     ====="
	sync
}
case "$1" in
	start) start ;;
	stop|restart) : ;;
	*) echo "Usage: $0 {start|stop|restart}"; exit 1 ;;
esac
exit 0
